# The word "saturated" is earned ONLY at red (banshee-87l.19). The reframe's whole
# point is that a red CPU reading now means MEASURED busy-time, so the finding may
# say the machine is saturated; a yellow or contention reading must not. Dropping
# "saturated: cores are" from the red-band message erases the one claim the finding
# exists to make, and the test that a red cpu names saturation (while yellow/held
# do not) fails.
file: rust/banshee-core/src/pressure/mod.rs
test: the_cpu_finding_claims_saturation_only_at_red
---OLD---
            format!("CPU is saturated: cores are {:.0}% busy.", r.value * 100.0)
---NEW---
            format!("CPU is {:.0}% busy.", r.value * 100.0)
